{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 0e674830e524a9c82321910accd65735c957236d. Read the design note first in full, then the qualification record. Four findings:\n\nF1 (P1), primary notes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md:202-209, also sections 3, 4.5, 5 and H4: the bucket-only backup model omits acknowledged state on node disks. In default fleet mode a response may precede bucket upload; pinned v0.6.2 requires recovery from surviving follower logs. A bucket version/replica alone can therefore omit acknowledged writes or leave an open recovery record whose required tail is unavailable when the two VMs are replaced. Document persistent node/follower data and identity, the safe stop/drain and backup boundary, and the limits of bucket-only restore; require the kit/qualification to preserve and recover acknowledged tails before claiming this backup/replacement model. The supervisor also needs unrestricted restart with at least a lease lifetime between attempts and sufficient stop grace. Sources: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/docs/guarantees.md (ensemble/recovery/supervisor); https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/docs/README.md (shutdown/upgrade). This is a missing design obligation, not a claim the one-node run lost data.\n\nF2 (P2), primary:87-92 and 315-319, companion qualification:200-203: the measurements do not bound or isolate the bucket proof. Recorded GCP-minus-laptop act p50 is 1076-571=505 ms, not 70-180 ms. GCP act p50 minus one different read is 178 ms; subtracting a health RTT from that does not establish a \u003c=70 ms commit cost. Different commands, unmatched samples, process startup, runtime work and transport remain confounded. Likewise 66 seconds of verify wall time does not prove the node contributed nothing. Keep the observed table and timings, remove the causal bounds and guaranteed two-node improvement, or label them unquantified hypotheses pending H4 instrumentation. Apply the correction to both documents, including section 6's claimed tens of milliseconds.\n\nF3 (P2), primary:117-120 versus 164-169: r2_buckets is explicitly excluded as an unsupported Cloudflare-only key, while package storage requires adding precisely that supported celld binding. Pinned celld accepts it and stores application bytes under r2/\u003cbucket_name\u003e/ in the fleet store. Correct the configuration contract: an optional APPLICATION_CONTENT R2 binding with its intended bucket_name/prefix and existing trust configuration, omitted only when packages are disabled. Note celld dev has no fleet bucket and R2 methods fail there; the two recorded smokes did not witness package storage. Name the cloud package get/conditional-put/readback witness in a later slice instead of treating the baseline dev smoke as package acceptance. Sources: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/docs/cloudflare-compat.md and https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/docs/services/r2.md; production packages/scope/src/applications/{bindings,content}.ts.\n\nF4 (P2), primary section 2 coupling table and 4.6: the client-address trust coupling is missing. packages/scope/src/worker.ts:320 passes cf-connecting-ip to JoinLimits; packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts:556 uses that header for bearer-failure limits. Pinned celld ingress copies input headers without injecting a trusted CF address, and a default Caddy reverse proxy passes non-forwarding headers through. A caller can therefore rotate the supplied header to evade both address limits; without it joins have no address window and MCP failures share the empty key. Add an ingress-owned client-address contract: overwrite the header from the verified connecting client, reject public bypass of that proxy, and preserve it to the hosted object. Give H1/H3 a concrete forged/missing-header and independent-client witness. This changes serving transport protection, not native judgments or history. Sources: pinned celld crates/celld/main.rs ingress_payload_parts (downloaded tag archive SHA-256 61c073fc91b26cedc9ba042e9112750657fefee3b442f72626045b159b79b71b); https://caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/reverse_proxy#headers.\n\nConclusions: the pinned celld/runtime direction and reuse of RegisterHost/DestinationHost behind recorded host self are coherent, with GitRepository a host object rather than a new native scope kind. Smart Git compatibility, durable token handling, repository/read bounds and independent archive custody remain H2/later witnesses; the memory OwnGit smoke proves none of those. The two-cloud kit and after-plan-033 order are reasonable, but the four corrections above must precede approval; two-node alarms/failover/TLS/upgrades/packages remain unqualified. Qualification claims were assessed against the committed narrative and pinned upstream code/docs, not independently rerun cloud infrastructure or unavailable raw run logs.\n\nValidation: all 2290 candidate leaves checked; all 2288 base leaves unchanged, exactly two added notes. Fourteen relative links resolve and git diff --check passes. Candidate tree e1b3ee9ad2f353e7cdc4b9654150dec9a4722ab4 versus base 9554919b/tree bbabe9a2f6e0d374b845b46f18d9856251ed0b57. Source and tests unchanged: no gate rerun under docs/testing.md's documentation-only exception. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-celld-design-dtwhk47a contains exact materialization, validation.json, checks.json and read-only pinned upstream source. No install, source/ref mutation, push or deployment by checker. Read H1 99918e60, H2 a3460956 and interactive planner steering401254ce in full; their dependency on design approval and plan033 remains intact.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ffb94adbc34c94fdaa37c07bc97c798e1f8ff2a9","binding":"assigned","head":"0e674830e524a9c82321910accd65735c957236d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4fcdfb6b28867961a88eaafb6e668acddba277a9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e9e4a685a8299cb897a2ea2d41c5b4873a4b3c92\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:401254ce7262de9c788df5e51b874fce49ed8343","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}